**Negative proof:** Not applicable to the verdict (DEFECTIVE), but recorded as verified negatives so the next pass need not re-derive them: (1) Published-surface hygiene HOLDS — no file in the card's dependency cone imports @mkbabb/value.js at all, the whole demo/palettes/ feature touches it exactly twice and both are correct published subpaths (mix.ts:14 and export/png.ts:11 → @mkbabb/value.js/color); `grep -rn 'from \"@mkbabb/value.js\"' demo/` returns ZERO bare-root imports, which matters because package.json#exports has no \".\" key, so a bare-root specifier would be one a real consumer could not write; no @src/*, no dist/*, no path alias anywhere in the six files. The T.W1 demo-dogfood keystone is intact. (2) verbatimModuleSyntax (edict 8) is CLEAN across all six files — PaletteCard.vue:168-169, PaletteCardMenu.vue:177-178, PaletteCardSwatches.vue:72, PaletteCardMeta.vue:59 all use `import type` or an inline `type` specifier. (3) No global keyframe is forked into a component — both scoped <style> blocks (PaletteCard.vue:337-364, ActionFeedback.vue:50-58) contain only geometry custom properties for the shared vj-morph / vj-celebrate families; the retired golden-text-shimmer fork is genuinely gone (edict 6 respected). (4) card/index.ts is a NAMED re-export barrel, not a star re-export — correct for SFCs whose scoped style makes the import side-effecting (PI-6). (5) useTemplateRef is used correctly at PaletteRenameInput.vue:48. (6) PaletteColorStrip.vue (72 L) carries no colour maths and no glass-ui edge — vue + own types only. (7) useHoverPopover.close() is bypassed at four sites in PaletteCard.vue (277, 322, 327, 332) which null openPopoverIndex without cancelling the leave timer; I traced every re-open path (onHover, onSwatchClick) and each calls cancelLeave() first, so the divergence is currently BENIGN — recorded as an unowned invariant, deliberately NOT filed as a defect.

## Defects (10)

### L-15 — BLOCKER

`.floating-panel` — the class that is supposed to make the swatch hover popover a floating surface — is defined by NO module: not in demo/styles/, not anywhere in the repo's CSS, not in @mkbabb/glass-ui 7.0.0. The teleported popover therefore computes to position:static with no background, shadow or z-index, so its inline top/left are inert and it lands in normal flow at the end of <body>.

- **Evidence:** SwatchHoverMenu.vue:37-51 applies `class="floating-panel"` + inline :style. `grep -rn "floating-panel" --include='*.css' . --exclude-dir=node_modules` → one hit, and it is a COMMENT (demo/styles/animations.css:2). `grep -rln "floating-panel" node_modules/@mkbabb/` → no output. Live probe (synthetic element + full document.styleSheets scan): {"computed":{"position":"static","transform":"none","background":"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)","zIndex":"auto","border":"0px","boxShadow":"none"},"rules":[],"ruleCount":0}. Measured rendered geometry: rect {x:-720, y:900, w:1440, h:40}, parentIsBody:true. Spec: CSS Positioned Layout L3, `static` — "the box's top, right, bottom, and left properties have no effect."
- **Mechanism:** Ownership vacuum / dangling design-system reference. Glass 7.0.0 was 'adopted whole' at W44; `.floating-panel` was a glass-ui recipe the demo never owned and glass-ui 7 does not ship. No toolchain can see it — a CSS class is a string.
- **Reproduction:** http://localhost:9000/#/palettes with ≥1 saved palette in localStorage key `color-palettes` → click a card to expand → hover any swatch. Popover renders as a transparent full-viewport-width strip at the bottom of the document instead of a panel over the swatch.
- **Proposed cure:** Delete the hand-rolled hover branch entirely. glass-ui 7 ships ./popover and SwatchHoverMenu ALREADY uses it on the touch branch (line 61). Fold the swatch + its popover into ONE glass-ui `Swatch` component that owns its own surface; `.floating-panel` ceases to exist rather than being redefined in demo/.

### L-16 — BLOCKER

useHoverPopover reads `e.currentTarget` inside a nextTick callback — i.e. after event dispatch has completed, when the DOM spec guarantees it is null. Every swatch hover throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'getBoundingClientRect')` and the popover's position is never applied. The `as Element` cast is the masking assertion that hid it from vue-tsc.

- **Evidence:** demo/palettes/browser/card/composables/useHoverPopover.ts:30 — `nextTick(() => positionPanel(e.currentTarget as Element));`. Live capture with an unhandledrejection listener: {"captured":["REJ:TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'getBoundingClientRect')"],"inline":"top: 0px; left: 0px; transform: translateX(-50%);"} — the inline top/left are still the reactive initial 0px, proving positionPanel never completed. Spec: DOM Standard §2.2 — "The currentTarget attribute … When an event is dispatched, this is set to the object whose listener is being invoked, and reset to null afterwards."
- **Mechanism:** Hand-rolled floating positioning inside a demo composable, duplicating @mkbabb/glass-ui/popover which the same component already imports and uses on its other branch. A dual path (edict 2) reimplementing a design-system primitive (edict 4); the `as Element` cast (edict 2 — masking fallback) let the null flow through typecheck.
- **Reproduction:** http://localhost:9000/#/palettes, seed one palette, expand the card, dispatch/perform pointerenter on a swatch wrapper with `window.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', …)` installed. The rejection fires on every hover, on every desktop browser (canHover = matchMedia('(hover: hover)')).
- **Proposed cure:** Capture the element at dispatch time (`const el = e.currentTarget as Element` BEFORE nextTick) is the patch; the transposition is to delete the branch — let the design-system Popover anchor to its own trigger so no coordinate is ever computed in demo/ at all.

### L-17 — MAJOR

The swatches pass `tag="button"` and `:aria-label` to glass-ui 7's WatercolorDot, which declares neither. Both are silently dropped: every colour swatch renders as `<span aria-hidden="true">`. The only focusable element in an expanded PaletteCard is the 'Palette menu' button — the card's primary content is keyboard-unreachable and invisible to assistive technology.

- **Evidence:** SwatchHoverMenu.vue:14-20 and :29-36 pass tag="button" + :aria-label; CurrentPaletteEditor.vue:62,64,95-105 the same. glass-ui 7.0.0 contract (node_modules/@mkbabb/glass-ui/dist/components/watercolor-dot/WatercolorDot.vue.d.ts): `type __VLS_Props = { color: string; variant?: "solid"|"ghost"; animate?: boolean; cycleDuration?: number; range?: [number,number]; seed?: string; }` — no `tag`, no name plumbing. Live DOM: {"tag":"SPAN","attrs":{"aria-hidden":"true","data-testid":"watercolor-swatch","data-variant":"solid", …no aria-label, no tabindex},"focusablesInCard":["BUTTON:Palette menu"]}.
- **Mechanism:** Stale design-system prop contract surviving the Glass-7 adoption. vue-tsc cannot catch it: unknown attributes on a component are legal fallthrough attrs, not prop errors — so a green typecheck is not evidence the contract is current.
- **Reproduction:** http://localhost:9000/#/palettes, seed a palette, expand the card, then query the swatch element's attributes and the card's focusable set: `[...card.querySelectorAll('a[href],button,input,select,textarea,[tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])')]` returns exactly one entry, the menu button.
- **Proposed cure:** The Swatch belongs in glass-ui as a first-class component that renders a real <button> with an accessible name — not a WatercolorDot the consumer tries to retag from outside. Interim: stop passing props the DS does not declare and wrap the dot in a real button in SwatchHoverMenu.

